Project analysis (current structure)
•	Tech stack: .NET 8 Web API + MongoDB.
•	Main API project: MMPortalIntegrationApi.
•	Layers:
•	Controllers (integration + external API endpoints)
•	Services (business logic for Redmine, Vryno, PerfettoHR, Karyakeeper)
•	DataAccess (Mongo repositories)
•	Model / Dtos / Keys
•	Supported portal types (factory-based): Redmine, Vryno, PerfettoHR, Karyakeeper.
•	Auth patterns used:
•	X-Api-Key header for internal integration endpoints.
•	JWT Bearer token for external endpoints like AttendanceController.
•	External dependency: Mera Monitor APIs from MeraMonitorApi.BaseUri and ExternalBaseUri.
---
Step-by-step prerequisites for portal integration project
1.	Install runtime/tools
•	.NET SDK 8
•	MongoDB access (network + credentials)
•	Valid HTTPS dev certificate for local run
2.	Configure appsettings.json
•	ConnectionStrings:PortalIntegrationConnectionString
•	MongoDbName
•	Collection keys:
•	PortalIntegrationCollection
•	ExternalOrganizationMapperCollection
•	PortalOrgApiConfigCollection
•	AuthClientsCollection
•	others used by sync history/mappers
•	IssuerSigningKey, EncryptionKey, EncryptionIV
•	PortalIntegrationApiKey (required in X-Api-Key for many APIs)
•	MeraMonitorApi:BaseUri and MeraMonitorApi:ExternalBaseUri
3.	Seed master portal configuration data
•	Add active records in PortalConfiguration collection for each portal (PortalName, PortalURL, MMApiKey, MMPortalId, etc.).
•	Important: NewOrganizationSetup checks portal by PortalName; if not found, setup fails.
4.	Run API
•	Use https profile (launchSettings.json shows local ports).
•	Swagger is available in development at:
•	/internal-swagger-aapna-integration-portal
5.	Register client credentials (per organization)
•	Call: POST api/ClientManagement/RegisterClient
•	Header: X-Api-Key = PortalIntegrationApiKey
•	Body: organizationId
•	Save client_id and client_secret.
6.	Generate JWT access token
•	Call: POST api/oauth/token
•	Form fields:
•	client_id
•	client_secret
•	redirect_uri = urn:ietf:wg:oauth:2.0:oob
•	grant_type = client_credentials
•	Use returned token for JWT-protected external APIs.
7.	Setup organization integration
•	Call: POST api/SyncPortalIntegration/NewOrganizationSetup
•	Provide PortalIntegrationRequest:
•	MmPortalId, PortalName, MmOrgId, AdminName, AdminPassword
•	This creates:
•	ExternalOrganizationMapper
•	PortalOrgApiConfig with auth token details
8.	For OAuth-based portals (e.g., Vryno), complete token flow
•	POST .../GetFormAuthUrl
•	POST .../GenerateAndSaveToken
•	This stores access/refresh token in PortalOrgApiConfig.
9.	Run sync operations
•	Example endpoints:
•	SyncPortalDataByOrganization
•	SyncPortalDataByUser
•	SyncUserTimeEntry
•	SyncTimeEntriesToRedmine
•	Include correct X-Api-Key in headers.
10.	Validate security/ops before production
•	Move secrets from appsettings.json to secure secret storage.
•	Restrict Swagger and debug behavior in non-dev environment.
•	Ensure Mongo logging sink connection and retention are production-safe.
